WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.538
Welcome to our video best practices for creating brand names and logos.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:06.000
Brand

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.560
names and logos can be powerful tools for sellers hoping to attract loyal

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:11.053
customers.

00:00:11.053 --> 00:00:15.000
They help customers recognize and remember products and

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.197
distinguish one brand's goods from another's.

00:00:17.197 --> 00:00:19.760
If you're a new brand in the

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:24.560
process of creating a brand name or logo, the most important thing to remember is

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.720
that it should represent your products.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.600
Brand names and logos come in all shapes

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:30.289
and sizes.

00:00:30.289 --> 00:00:34.420
There's no one way to create them but think carefully about the

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:39.120
products you sell and why customers might want to buy them before designing

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.274
your brand name or logo.

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:44.720
Ask what makes your products unique, valuable and

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:45.151
memorable.

00:00:45.151 --> 00:00:49.466
You'll also want to keep these best practices in mind.

00:00:49.466 --> 00:00:50.329
Stay simple.

00:00:50.329 --> 00:00:50.760
The

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:55.400
best brand names are often short, easy to pronounce and straightforward to spell.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.656
Make it memorable.

00:00:56.656 --> 00:01:01.680
Your brand name and logo should stand out and be easy to

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.120
recognize and recall.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.080
Stay descriptive.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:07.440
Coming up with highly creative names is

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:11.760
fun but if they're too abstract or complicated they can prevent customers

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.747
from easily understanding your brand and products.

00:01:14.747 --> 00:01:16.880
If you sell a particular

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:19.656
product you might want to include it in your name.

00:01:19.656 --> 00:01:21.600
If your goods are of a certain

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:26.044
quality or type choose language or images that make that clear.

00:01:26.044 --> 00:01:27.660
Create a brand name

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:32.626
or logo that helps customers attach meaning and value to your products.

00:01:32.626 --> 00:01:33.040
For

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:38.720
example, if your products are eco-friendly consider associated words and images.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.680
Finally, remember that if you're planning to sell your products in the

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:47.549
Amazon store using a logo it needs to include your brand name.

00:01:47.549 --> 00:01:48.360
Logos and

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:52.540
brand names also need to be permanently affixed to your products or packaging.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:57.540
These requirements help Amazon pair brands with the right products.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:58.040
There's

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:03.192
also a couple of things to avoid while creating your brand name or logo.

00:02:03.192 --> 00:02:03.560
You

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:08.129
don't want to use offensive or culturally inappropriate words or images.

00:02:08.129 --> 00:02:08.960
Be sure

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:13.240
you also understand what the words and images in your brand name and logo mean

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:18.360
to a variety of audiences especially if you're translating text to another

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:18.807
language.

00:02:18.807 --> 00:02:23.720
And avoid simply translating a brand name literally from one language

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:24.667
to another.

00:02:24.667 --> 00:02:29.400
Brand names are culturally specific and translating them word for

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:32.743
word often means losing or changing the original meaning.

00:02:32.743 --> 00:02:34.600
You also don't want to

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:38.623
create a name or logo that's too similar to a competitor's.

00:02:38.623 --> 00:02:39.720
That won't help

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:43.800
distinguish your products from theirs and it could lead to claims of trademark

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:48.248
infringement or other legal or intellectual property issues.

00:02:48.248 --> 00:02:49.360
Your brand

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:53.253
name and logo can use wordplay or newly invented words.

00:02:53.253 --> 00:02:55.200
They can evoke a feeling

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:55.806
or emotion.

00:02:55.806 --> 00:02:59.440
You can also stick to describing who you are and what you

00:02:59.440 --> 00:02:59.862
produce.

00:02:59.862 --> 00:03:04.920
However you choose to represent your products, take the time to brainstorm

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:07.789
and collect feedback on your brand name or logo.

00:03:07.789 --> 00:03:10.340
It can be a good idea to consult

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:13.237
a brand agency or other expert too.

00:03:13.237 --> 00:03:15.720
This concludes our best practices video.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:19.883
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store!
